* Methods

Go does not have classes.
However, you can define methods on types.

A method is a function with a special ⟪GTI18N_8a62096b_000001⟫receiver⟪GTI18N_8a62096b_000002⟫ argument.

The receiver appears in its own argument list between the ⟪GTI18N_8a62096b_000003⟫func⟪GTI18N_8a62096b_000004⟫ keyword and
the method name.

In this example, the ⟪GTI18N_8a62096b_000005⟫Abs⟪GTI18N_8a62096b_000006⟫ method has a receiver of type ⟪GTI18N_8a62096b_000007⟫Vertex⟪GTI18N_8a62096b_000008⟫ named ⟪GTI18N_8a62096b_000009⟫v⟪GTI18N_8a62096b_000010⟫.

